    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0370" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg56"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/397</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul General at Cairo</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Knabenshue</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-13T13:00:00+02:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 13, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3:30 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Referring to your cipher telegram August 12, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d128-f1"/> was informed to-day by the British Chargé d’Affaires that
                    Great Britain has declared war against Austria. Communications have ceased
                    between Egyptian Government and German diplomatic representative and consuls and
                    similar action will be taken with regard to Austrian representatives.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knabenshue</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
